# Generated model output. Everything here is reproducible from
# generate_loftbed.py via `mise run build` / `build-full` / `usdz` / `render*`,
# and the files are large and binary, so none of it belongs in git.
loftbed_*.step
loftbed_*.stl
loftbed_*.usdz
loftbed_*.glb
loftbed_*.png
loftbed_*.svg

# v1 (alcove frame) output, regenerated by `mise run build-alcove`.
bed_frame.step
bed_frame.bin

# The one generated MODEL file that IS tracked is parts.tsv - the regression
# snapshot of every part's bounding box. Do not ignore it.
#
# The generated DOCUMENTATION is tracked on purpose and must not be ignored:
#   docs/generated/*.md   the tables docs/ASSEMBLY.md links to
#   docs/MONTERING.md     the pictorial guide
#   docs/img/steg-*.*     one line drawing per build step
#   docs/img/hanna-hero.* the cover drawing
#   docs/img/beslag/      the fastener glyphs
#   docs/img/ikon/        the preparation pictograms
# They are rebuilt by `mise run build` and `mise run montering`, but the
# picture guide has to be readable (and printable) on a machine that has
# neither the Python toolchain nor rsvg-convert, so the output is committed
# rather than regenerated on demand.

# The shaded reference renders of the same steps are NOT tracked - they need
# the macOS USD tools, and the manual does not use them.
docs/img/skyggelagt/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store
